Implemented in [PR #65](https://github.com/johnnylarner/exposed/pull/65), committed as `8b6505b`.

`IntoResponse` now converts `String`, `&str`, `()`, custom output types, and `Result<T, E>` into a common `Response`. Commands return values, dispatch converts them, and the entrypoint writes the response.

```rust
impl IntoResponse for Imported {
    fn into_response(self) -> Response {
        format!("Imported {} records\n", self.0).into_response()
    }
}
```

Existing output text and error context are preserved. Model the Domain guided the single success-or-error representation. Boundary Discipline placed final output at the entrypoint.

Design exploration ran in parallel; one implementation owner handled the coupled changes. Independent review found no issues.

All 26 focused tests and two documentation examples pass. Full offline test compilation remains blocked by existing SQLx metadata gaps. Clippy reports six existing issues in unchanged files.

